  "interpretation": [
    "Toggle of the equality-implied redundant-bound removal rule changes the returned objective at identical raw starts and input hashes; this supports a controlled intervention effect within this computational protocol.",
    "Objective comparisons are conditional on both endpoints being certified. Six-common cohorts control cohort variation across R3/SS/HH.",
    "The normalized gap uses max(1,abs(f_keep),abs(f_remove)); some objectives are below 1, so it is not an ordinary percentage decrease. The latter is recomputed separately.",
    "Removing bounds lowers objectives for nearly every jointly certified case, while decreasing certified coverage of R3 and SS. HH keeps the same strict certified case set.",
    "Twenty-two records are indeterminate due to controller interruption and unavailable resources; these must not be relabelled numerical failures.",
    "No Ipopt reference objective is in the paired CSV. Quantifying closure of the Lazy/Ipopt gap needs a frozen-reference join on case/input/start binding.",
    "This is a parallel 22-worker campaign with one observation per cell, not a quiet three-repetition timing study; avoid causal runtime or global-optimality claims."
  ],
